                "text": "Master of the world, fulfil our wishes for the good, grant our will and give us our wish; forgive all our sins and all the sins of our household through forgiveness in grace and forgiveness in mercy and purify us from our transgressions, sins and iniquities; remember us benevolently before Thee and consider us with salvation and compassion; remember us for a long and good life, for peace, livelihood and sustenance; give us bread to eat, clothes to wear, wealth and honour, long life to ponder on Thy Torah and fulfil its commandments and sense and intelligence, to grasp and understand the depths of its mysteries. Send healing for all our sufferings, bless all the work of our hands, decree for us good decrees, help and comfort; annul all harsh decrees from upon us, incline the heart of the kingdom, its advisers and princes for our good, Amen. Thus may it be Thy will."
